# The body of a constructor function is copied in the place of `new`, for the object that the walk has just made. If that were asked for no window in a copy, each level would be copied into each copy of the level above:
# eight to the n frames: at eight levels the build ran for two minutes and stopped at a limit of the compiler. In a copy it is copied within the window of the call that the unit's own body writes, as every copy in a copy.
# f5 = L4: 8 + 64 + 512 + 4,096 frames without the window
# RUN: walk f5 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: frame 8 callee=f4
# CHECK-NOT: frame 100 callee=
